				<r3d:description language="eng">&lt;&lt;&lt;!!!&lt;&lt;&lt; The demand for high-value environmental data and information has dramatically increased in recent years. To improve our ability to meet that demand, NOAA’s former three data centers—the National Climatic Data Center, the National Geophysical Data Center, and the National Oceanographic Data Center, which includes the National Coastal Data Development Center—have merged into the National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI).  https://www.re3data.org/repository/r3d100011801 &gt;&gt;&gt;!!!&gt;&gt;&gt;
NOAA&#039;s National Climatic Data Center (NCDC) is responsible for preserving, monitoring, assessing, and providing public access to the Nation&#039;s treasure of climate and historical weather data and information.</r3d:description>
